00:08:00,940 --> 00:08:04,980
So in today's dialogue, we heard Mr. Ford talk about some numbers.

94
00:08:05,260 --> 00:08:08,040
He's talking about growth and change in the market.

95
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:16,880
And he says with figures to around 4-5%, we've got an overall increase of 1000%.

96
00:08:16,880 --> 00:08:17,040
That's right.

97
00:08:17,880 --> 00:08:21,000
So what's a phrase, an increase of?

98
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:29,120
Very very common when you're talking about growth of maybe revenue or when you're talking about the growth of a company or sales for example.

99
00:08:29,120 --> 00:08:32,080
So it's important to remember here that this is a fixed phrase.

100
00:08:32,080 --> 00:08:37,680
We say an increase of 10% or an increase of 30%.

101
00:08:37,680 --> 00:08:43,960
But you can use the same phrase with drops in percentages or money.

102
00:08:44,200 --> 00:08:46,860
So you can say a decrease of 10%.

103
00:08:46,860 --> 00:08:50,820
That means that you go down 10% or a decrease of 100%.

104
00:08:50,820 --> 00:08:51,460
That's right.

105
00:08:51,960 --> 00:09:00,040
So a very useful phrase when talking about incrementing someone or as you said, decreasing it, decrease of 5%.

