129
00:10:04,200 --> 00:10:08,340
So we're talking about the X420 computer brand itself.

130
00:10:08,740 --> 00:10:12,920
Now what does Mr. Ford mean when he says to compare and contrast?

131
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:21,180
So when we mention the word compare, we are basically trying to determine how they are similar in many ways, the characteristics of how they are similar.

132
00:10:22,120 --> 00:10:25,800
And to contrast is how they are different, right?

133
00:10:25,800 --> 00:10:26,800
That's right.

134
00:10:26,800 --> 00:10:27,520
So let's use an example.

135
00:10:28,720 --> 00:10:31,520
Perhaps we could say Pepsi and Coca-Cola.

136
00:10:31,520 --> 00:10:32,640
Let's compare and contrast.

137
00:10:33,970 --> 00:10:36,110
So they're both carbonated beverages.

138
00:10:37,050 --> 00:10:37,910
They are both sweet.

139
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:41,840
And they're both, they're pretty much the same color.

140
00:10:41,840 --> 00:10:42,010
That's right.

141
00:10:42,840 --> 00:10:43,910
And they're also fairly cheap.

142
00:10:44,520 --> 00:10:46,000
They have about the same price.

143
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:51,360
But I would say that Coca-Cola tastes more like prune.

144
00:10:51,360 --> 00:10:56,090
So that would be a contrasting characteristic of Coca-Cola is that maybe it tastes a little bit sweeter.

145
00:10:56,460 --> 00:10:56,780
It does.

146
00:10:57,600 --> 00:11:00,240
And you could also say it's easier to find Coca-Cola.

147
00:11:00,300 --> 00:11:02,560
Pepsi is less easy to find sometimes.

148
00:11:02,880 --> 00:11:03,280
That's right.

149
00:11:03,420 --> 00:11:04,240
Another way that they're different.

150
00:11:04,620 --> 00:11:09,560
To compare and contrast is to point out how two things are similar and how they're different.

151
00:11:09,880 --> 00:11:10,420
That's right.

